                            	  1682:     ; Submode 1.
                            	  1683:     ; Copies the whole play area to NT 0, one row each frame.
                            	  1684:     ;
                            	  1685:     ; TODO:
                            	  1686:     ; If mode 7 scrolls to a dark room, then it sets
                            	  1687:     ; CurRow to zero. Otherwise it would be $FF.
                            	  1688:     ; A positive value triggers this submode 1 to transfer
                            	  1689:     ; the whole play area.
                            	  1690:     ;
                            	  1691:     ; But why? As far as I can tell, the NT 0 is already in
                            	  1692:     ; a good state reflecting the new room. The only thing
                            	  1693:     ; needed is possibly to brighten the room by way of
                            	  1694:     ; changing the palette.
                            	  1695:     ;
                            	  1696:     ; So why does mode 7 trigger this?
                            	  1697:     ; Is there another mode that truly needs this behavior?
                            	  1698:     ;
02:00041070 102C00E9        	  1699:     move.b  ($00E9,A4),D0
02:00041074 6B06            	  1700:     bmi  _anon_z05_40
02:00041076 61003660        	  1701:     jsr     CopyNextRowToTransferBuf
